From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 10:24:12 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] mtld3d: the facade's winemetal structs on i686 Linux too (old
 WoW64)

An i686 mtld3d.so (old WoW64's 32-bit Unix side in the VM's guest) talks
to an i686 winemetal.so that takes DXMT's i386 layouts, the x86_64 ones.
Rust gives i686 Linux a 4-byte u64 and pointer: winemetal's memory
pointers are wmt::Ptr (8 bytes, the upper half 0 in a 32-bit process),
structs the C side aligns to 8 say align(8), and the draw nodes and
NewTextureView spell out the C padding; the scissor node takes u64s
rather than objc2's NSUInteger. The x86_64 and aarch64 layouts don't
change. The shared crate's u64 alignment probe skips i686 Linux, where
MacNeutron's mtld3d-layout32-check.sh compares every repr(C) struct of
the shared crate and the facade with the x86_64 build's (132 structs).

Assisted-by: Claude Code: claude-opus-5-5
